{"strategy": "always-large", "item_id": "xbinary-03", "category": "xbinary", "difficulty": "xhard", "ts": 1791924954.321093, "latency_ms": 6018.3, "retries": 0, "http_status": 200, "status": "ok", "passed": true, "detail": "got '101001000011000000110000011101'", "model": "groq-gpt-oss-120b", "tier": "large", "attempts": 1, "prompt_tokens": 102, "completion_tokens": 2599, "shadow_cost_usd": 0.0015747, "response": "**Step‑by‑step conversion**\n\n1. Find the highest power of 2 ≤ 688 655 389.  \n   \\(2^{29}=536 870 912\\) is the largest such power.\n\n2. Subtract successive powers of 2, recording a 1 when the power fits, otherwise 0:\n\n| Power (2^k) | Subtract? | Remaining |\n|-------------|-----------|-----------|\n| 2^29 | 1 | 151 784 477 |\n| 2^28 | 0 | 151 784 477 |\n| 2^27 | 1 | 17 566 749 |\n| 2^26 | 0 | 17 566 749 |\n| 2^25 | 0 | 17 566 749 |\n| 2^24 | 1 | 789 533 |\n| 2^23‑2^20 | 0 | 789 533 |\n| 2^19 | 1 | 265 245 |\n| 2^18 | 1 | 3 101 |\n| 2^17‑2^12 | 0 | 3 101 |\n| 2^11 | 1 | 1 053 |\n| 2^10 | 1 | 29 |\n| 2^9‑2^5 | 0 | 29 |\n| 2^4 | 1 | 13 |\n| 2^3 | 1 | 5 |\n| 2^2 | 1 | 1 |\n| 2^1 | 0 | 1 |\n| 2^0 | 1 | 0 |\n\n3. Reading the bits from \\(2^{29}\\) down to \\(2^{0}\\) gives:\n\n\\[\n101001000011000000110000011101\n\\]\n\n(30 bits; the leading zeros are omitted.)\n\n**Answer:** 101001000011000000110000011101", "response_truncated": false}
