{"strategy": "always-large", "item_id": "xmodpow-03", "category": "xmodpow", "difficulty": "xhard", "ts": 1791924962.502524, "latency_ms": 5087.8, "retries": 0, "http_status": 200, "status": "ok", "passed": true, "detail": "got 144, want 144", "model": "groq-gpt-oss-120b", "tier": "large", "attempts": 1, "prompt_tokens": 108, "completion_tokens": 1993, "shadow_cost_usd": 0.001212, "response": "**Step 1: Factor the modulus**\n\n\\(1395 = 5 \\times 9 \\times 31\\) (the factors are pairwise coprime).\n\n**Step 2: Compute the remainder modulo each factor**\n\n*Modulo 5*  \n\\(423 \\equiv 3 \\pmod 5\\).  \n\\(3^{4906}\\equiv 3^{4906\\bmod 4}=3^{2}=9\\equiv 4\\pmod5\\).\n\n*Modulo 9*  \n\\(423 = 9\\cdot 47\\), so \\(423\\equiv0\\pmod9\\).  \nThus \\(423^{4906}\\equiv0\\pmod9\\).\n\n*Modulo 31*  \n\\(423\\equiv20\\pmod{31}\\).  \nSince \\(\\phi(31)=30\\), reduce the exponent: \\(4906\\bmod30 = 16\\).  \nCompute \\(20^{16}\\pmod{31}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n20^2 &\\equiv 28 \\pmod{31}\\\\\n20^4 &\\equiv 28^2 \\equiv 9 \\pmod{31}\\\\\n20^8 &\\equiv 9^2 \\equiv 19 \\pmod{31}\\\\\n20^{16}&\\equiv 19^2 \\equiv 20 \\pmod{31}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nHence \\(423^{4906}\\equiv20\\pmod{31}\\).\n\n**Step 3: Combine the congruences with the Chinese Remainder Theorem**\n\nWe need \\(x\\) such that  \n\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\nx\\equiv4\\pmod5,\\\\\nx\\equiv0\\pmod9,\\\\\nx\\equiv20\\pmod{31}.\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nFirst combine the mod 5 and mod 9 conditions:\n\n\\(x\\equiv0\\pmod9\\) ⇒ \\(x=9k\\).  \n\\(9k\\equiv4\\pmod5\\) ⇒ \\(4k\\equiv4\\pmod5\\) ⇒ \\(k\\equiv1\\pmod5\\).  \nThus \\(k=1+5t\\) and \\(x=9+45t\\). So \\(x\\equiv9\\pmod{45}\\).\n\nNow combine with the mod 31 condition:\n\n\\(x=9+45m\\).  \n\\(9+45m\\equiv20\\pmod{31}\\) ⇒ \\(14m\\equiv11\\pmod{31}\\).  \nThe inverse of \\(14\\) modulo \\(31\\) is \\(20\\) (since \\(14\\cdot20\\equiv1\\pmod{31}\\)).  \nHence \\(m\\equiv20\\cdot11\\equiv220\\equiv3\\pmod{31}\\).\n\nTake \\(m=3+31t\\). Then  \n\n\\[\nx = 9 + 45(3+31t)=144 + 1395t.\n\\]\n\nThe smallest non‑negative remainder is therefore \\(x=144\\).\n\n**Answer:** 144.", "response_truncated": false}
