{"strategy": "always-cheapest", "item_id": "xmodpow-02", "category": "xmodpow", "difficulty": "xhard", "ts": 1791924994.343885, "latency_ms": 4865.0, "retries": 0, "http_status": 200, "status": "ok", "passed": true, "detail": "got 39987, want 39987", "model": "groq-gpt-oss-20b", "tier": "small", "attempts": 1, "prompt_tokens": 107, "completion_tokens": 3873, "shadow_cost_usd": 0.00116993, "response": "To find the remainder of \\(717^{229}\\) when divided by \\(81459\\), we use the Chinese Remainder Theorem.\n\n**1. Factor the modulus**\n\n\\[\n81459 = 3^3 \\times 7 \\times 431 = 27 \\times 7 \\times 431\n\\]\n\n**2. Compute the power modulo each factor**\n\n- Mod \\(27\\):\n  \\[\n  717 \\equiv 15 \\pmod{27}\n  \\]\n  \\(15^3 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{27}\\), so \\(15^{229} \\equiv 0 \\pmod{27}\\).\n\n- Mod \\(7\\):\n  \\[\n  717 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{7}\n  \\]\n  \\(\\phi(7)=6\\), \\(229 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{6}\\), thus \\(3^{229} \\equiv 3 \\pmod{7}\\).\n\n- Mod \\(431\\):\n  \\[\n  717 \\equiv 286 \\pmod{431}\n  \\]\n  Since \\(\\gcd(286,431)=1\\) and \\(\\phi(431)=430\\), we compute \\(286^{229}\\pmod{431}\\) by repeated squaring:\n  \\[\n  286^{229} \\equiv 335 \\pmod{431}\n  \\]\n\n**3. Combine the congruences**\n\nWe need \\(x\\) such that\n\n\\[\nx \\equiv 0 \\pmod{27},\\quad\nx \\equiv 3 \\pmod{7},\\quad\nx \\equiv 335 \\pmod{431}.\n\\]\n\nFirst combine the first two:\n\nLet \\(x = 27k\\).  \n\\(27k \\equiv 3 \\pmod{7}\\Rightarrow 6k \\equiv 3 \\pmod{7}\\Rightarrow k \\equiv 4 \\pmod{7}\\).\n\nThus \\(x \\equiv 108 \\pmod{189}\\).\n\nNow combine with the modulus \\(431\\):\n\nLet \\(x = 108 + 189t\\).  \n\\(108 + 189t \\equiv 335 \\pmod{431}\\Rightarrow 189t \\equiv 227 \\pmod{431}\\).\n\nThe inverse of \\(189\\) modulo \\(431\\) is \\(187\\) (since \\(189\\cdot187 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{431}\\)).  \nHence \\(t \\equiv 227\\cdot187 \\equiv 211 \\pmod{431}\\).\n\nSo \\(t = 211 + 431k\\) and\n\n\\[\nx = 108 + 189(211 + 431k) = 39987 + 81459k.\n\\]\n\nThus the unique remainder modulo \\(81459\\) is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{39987}\n\\]", "response_truncated": false}
{"strategy": "always-cheapest", "item_id": "xmult-03", "category": "xmult", "difficulty": "xhard", "ts": 1791925056.842255, "latency_ms": 2461.6, "retries": 0, "http_status": 200, "status": "ok", "passed": true, "detail": "got 3.5591e+07, want 35590964", "model": "groq-gpt-oss-20b", "tier": "small", "attempts": 1, "prompt_tokens": 102, "completion_tokens": 622, "shadow_cost_usd": 0.00019425, "response": "To multiply 28,772 by 1,237, break 1,237 into parts:\n\n1,237 = 1,200 + 37  \n\n**Step 1:**  \n28,772 × 1,200  \n= 28,772 × 12 × 100  \n= (28,772 × 10 + 28,772 × 2) × 100  \n= (287,720 + 57,544) × 100  \n= 345,264 × 100  \n= 34,526,400  \n\n**Step 2:**  \n28,772 × 37  \n= 28,772 × (30 + 7)  \n= (28,772 × 30) + (28,772 × 7)  \n= 863,160 + 201,404  \n= 1,064,564  \n\n**Step 3:**  \nAdd the two partial products:  \n34,526,400 + 1,064,564 = 35,590,964  \n\nAnswer: 35590964", "response_truncated": false}
